codex
The contraction currently pays for a large `[B,H,N,N] -> [B,N,N,H]` contiguous transpose before the second layernorm. I’ll test a Triton kernel that reads the batched-matmul output in `[B,H,N,N]` layout and directly writes the normalized/gated hidden tensor, eliminating that transpose and FP32 intermediate.
